<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Democratic Kampuchea</h1><p class="st-meta">1975 CE – 1979 CE · capital Phnom Penh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Khmer Rouge state of Pol Pot, whose radical communist experiment killed some 1.5 to 2 million Cambodians between 1975 and 1979.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Communist Party of Kampuchea</a>, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge, grew from a small insurgency in the 1960s to a large army during the civil war against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khmer-republic">Khmer Republic</a>. It captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> on 17 April 1975 and proclaimed Democratic <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia">Kampuchea</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Sihanouk</a> briefly as nominal head of state until 1976.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pol-pot">Pol Pot</a>, emptied the cities, abolished money, markets, schools and religion, and forced the population into agricultural communes. Former officials, intellectuals, ethnic minorities such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> and Vietnamese, and party members accused of treachery were executed, many after torture at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuol-sleng">Tuol Sleng</a> prison. Starvation, overwork and disease caused most of the deaths.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Border attacks on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Vietnam</a> provoked a Vietnamese invasion in December 1978, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> fell on 7 January 1979, when the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-republic-of-kampuchea">People's Republic of Kampuchea</a> was established. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> fought on from the Thai border into the 1990s, and a UN-backed tribunal later convicted surviving leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/democratic-kampuchea.jpg" alt="Democratic Kampuchea" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: This (SVG on base of source) was created by me. See File History, below, for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Democratic_Kampuchea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1975 CE – 1979 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phnom Penh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pol Pot, Khieu Samphan, Nuon Chea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khmer</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khmer Rouge regime</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1977&amp;focus=democratic-kampuchea" aria-label="Democratic Kampuchea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7566 1746 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Democratic Kampuchea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7886 2002L7886 2002M7886 2002L7846 1656M7886 2002L7886 2002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7886 2002h0M7846 1656h0M7886 2002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7886 2002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7886 2002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Phnom Penh. <a href="/atlas?year=1977&amp;focus=democratic-kampuchea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
